$string['aiopen'] = 'Open the reformulation aid to candidates';
$string['aiopen_desc'] = 'Closed by default. Open it only when the legal basis, the register, the retention and the contract with the AI provider are written (T-84), and the site\'s AI policy text and the instruction sent have been read by an accompanying person in VAE and by whoever keeps the data-protection register. Even open, a candidate needs the capability tool/vae:useai, given by hand (no role holds it by default; a site administrator passes every capability check, so the setting is the real lock), and a provider set up in the site administration (AI). The text a candidate sends and the answer are kept by the core in its own tables; this plugin erases none of them itself. Moodle empties them only when a person approves a data deletion request (the one Moodle files when an account is deleted, or the candidate\'s own), and on two conditions. First, Moodle files the request on its own: Site administration > Users > Privacy and policies > Privacy settings, "Create automatic data deletion requests" (otherwise nothing files it when an account is deleted). Second, the site\'s purpose and category are NOT defined in the data registry (same menu, "Data registry"): once they are, Moodle never empties these texts, even when the request is approved and declared done, and they have to be erased by hand. When either condition fails, the confirmation screen tells the candidate that Moodle does not erase them by itself. In every case Moodle keeps a line of its register: the account number, the date, the provider, the model, the size of the exchange (in tokens), the success or the failure of the call and, after a failure, the error message of the provider. The provider also receives the instruction configured in the AI settings: have it read with the instruction of this plugin.';
