$string['backupdossierintro'] = 'The backup is the dossier\'s normative archive, kept in your private files, folder vae, with no time limit. It survives the uninstallation of this plugin and is reimported with "Reimport an archive", unless a warning pointed out a line whose format is not the one expected (for example the rank of a competency written in lower case): the backup is then made all the same, but it cannot be reimported as it stands. Nor can it be reimported if, since the plugin was reinstalled, a dossier has already left the site on the same competencies (archive, Word or OpenDocument copy, backup), or if the account of the candidate has already been given a new identifier (with its first declaration, export, copy or backup): the site then gave them new numbers, the import is refused as a whole, and the message says why. Every dossier is also backed up this way, automatically, when the plugin is uninstalled. While the plugin is installed, the backup is deleted if the candidate asks for their data to be erased, even renamed or moved, but not a copy of it that you made. Once the plugin is uninstalled, nothing erases it any more: delete it by hand on request (its file name carries the candidate\'s identifier). It does not carry the deposits, the opinions, the requests for clarification, the earlier versions of the sections, nor the reflective journal and the preparation of the validation dossier, which no backup holds: a reimport does not bring them back.';
