$string['exportreadmeabsent'] = 'This archive is not a copy of the database. It does not carry, and a reimport therefore does not bring back: the deposits of the dossier de faisabilité (number, date, digest, notes), the opinions of the managers, the requests for clarification and their answers, the earlier versions of the sections (only the latest saved version of each is here), who decided the carry-over of a declaration and the note they wrote, and the tick "pieces read" of a signatory.';
$string['exportreadmeabsentauthor'] = 'It does not carry the reflective journal nor the preparation of the validation dossier either: only the archive that their author exports themself holds them, and no backup does.';
$string['exportreadmeabsentstructure'] = 'The positioning of the structure (evaluations and certifications) is not in this archive: it is no part of the dossier of the vaeiste. It is the object of a separate archive, the one of the accompanying structure, which the vaeiste may attach as an annex to their validation dossier.';
$string['exportreadmecontents'] = 'Contents: manifeste.json, the inventory of the archive with the SHA-256 digest of every file; preuves/, one declaration per file, in the format described by schema/preuve.schema.json; referentiel.json, the certification records and the labels of the competencies claimed, with their licence and attribution; faisabilite.json, validation.json, reflexion.json, hors_activite.json and pieces.json, each only when the dossier holds what it describes and the person who took the archive may carry it; schema/, the schemas of these files; dossier.pdf, the same dossier laid out for printing, which a reimport ignores.';
$string['exportreadmeintro'] = 'VAE dossier of {$a->name}, exported on {$a->date}. This archive is a frozen version of the dossier: it reads without the platform that produced it.';
$string['exportreadmepieces'] = 'pieces.json lists the supporting pieces attached to the declarations: nature, type, size, SHA-256 digest, dates, and the signature that covered each. The archive that the candidate exports themself, and the backup kept on the platform, also carry the files (pieces/, named by the identifier of the piece), the addresses of the links and the titles; an export made by anyone else carries none of them. The platform cannot check that a piece names nobody. A plugin older than version 0.39.0 reimports the declarations and loses the pieces without saying so.';
$string['exportreadmepositioning'] = 'positionnement.json holds the positionings of the structure: the evaluations of the competencies by the managers who follow the candidate and the certifications of the blocs by the direction, every line with its reason, its date and its fingerprint, the one that stands marked. It is not a validation: only the jury validates, outside the platform. A correction or a withdrawal made after this export has no effect on this archive. A plugin older than the one that wrote this file reimports the declarations and loses this file without saying so.';
$string['exportreadmeselfpos'] = 'autopositionnement.json holds the self-positioning of the vaeiste: where they themselves say they stand on each element of their record, at every level, by a step of a scale in words, with their optional justification, every line dated, the one that stands marked. It is their own word, not a validation and not a mark: only the jury validates, outside the platform, and nothing is computed from these lines. A plugin older than the one that wrote this file reimports the declarations and loses this file without saying so.';
$string['exportreadmesituations'] = 'situations.json holds the work situations of the vaeiste: for each, its title, its period, its setting, its tags (the elements of the record it is said to show), every version of its text with what each carried, the draft in progress if there is one, and its pieces; the list of those pieces; the annotations written by the managers the vaeiste consented to, withdrawals included; and the lines of that consent. The archive the vaeiste exports themself, and the backup kept on the platform, also carry the files (pieces-situations/, named by the identifier of the piece), the addresses of the links and the titles of the pieces; an export made by anyone else carries none of them. Nothing here is attested or validated: it is the word of the vaeiste about their work and, apart from it, the word of managers; only the jury validates, outside the platform. An annotation or a consent restored from an archive names no account of the site and opens no annotation. A plugin older than the one that wrote this file reimports the declarations and loses this file without saying so.';
$string['exportreadmeverify'] = 'The SHA-256 digests listed in manifeste.json detect a file damaged or changed by mistake; they do not prove where the archive comes from, since whoever changes a file can rewrite its digest too. To confirm that this archive is the one the platform issued, ask that platform, quoting the archive identifier {$a}: it keeps the digest of manifeste.json in its register and can say whether this copy matches it.';
$string['exportreadmewarning'] = 'WARNING. This archive holds at least one line whose format is not the one described by the schema in schema/. It was produced all the same, so that the dossier could be handed to the panel on time, but it cannot be reimported as it stands, and a tool that validates the schema will refuse it. The line comes from a declaration recorded with a competency rank outside the format, either by an earlier version of the plugin or directly in the database. It cannot be corrected from Moodle: the administrator of the platform that produced the archive should be told. Lines concerned:';
$string['exportwarning'] = 'The archive has been produced, but it holds at least one line whose format is not the one expected: it cannot be reimported as it stands. The line comes from a declaration recorded with a competency rank outside the format, either by an earlier version of the plugin or directly in the database. It cannot be corrected from Moodle: tell the site administrator. This warning will come back at every export for as long as the declaration exists. The editable copy of the dossier (Word or OpenDocument) remains possible, from the dossier. Lines concerned:';
$string['exportwarningemptyvalue'] = '(empty)';
$string['exportwarningitem'] = 'Declaration {$a->declaration} (record {$a->fiche}): file {$a->file}, field {$a->field}, value "{$a->value}".';
