$string['importdossierdone'] = 'Dossier rebuilt: {$a->declarations} declaration(s), {$a->attestations} attestation(s), {$a->rubriques} section(s) of the feasibility file restored, {$a->rubriquesgardees} left as they were; {$a->validation} section(s) of the preparation of the validation dossier restored, {$a->validationgardees} left as they were; {$a->reflexion} journal entry(ies) restored, {$a->reflexiongardees} left as they were; {$a->pieces} supporting piece(s) restored, {$a->piecesleft} not restored (the archive carries neither file nor address for them, as an export made by a third party does, or attaching is closed here and they are only listed); {$a->horsactivite} competency(ies) said to be outside the activity restored, {$a->horsactivitelaissees} left as they were or not held here.';
$string['importdossierforeign'] = 'This archive was not issued by this platform, or its identifier was changed: its authenticity cannot be verified here. Its digests only show that its files match its own manifest. To have it confirmed, ask the platform that issued it about the archive {$a}.';
$string['importdossierintro'] = 'Rebuild this dossier from an archive exported from this site or another one. Every file is checked against its SHA-256 digest and every declaration against the schema before anything is written; the slightest fault refuses the whole archive. The certification records the declarations refer to must have been imported first. The archive of another site is taken in only if this site has not already numbered differently the competencies it names, which happens for instance once a dossier on those competencies has left this site (archive, Word or OpenDocument copy, backup), and if the account of the candidate holds no identifier on this site yet (it gets one with its first declaration, export, copy or backup); otherwise it is refused as a whole, the message says why, and nothing is imported. An archive never carries the deposits of the feasibility dossier, the opinions of the managers or the questions for clarification: they do not come back.';
$string['importdossierpositioning'] = 'Positionings of the structure: {$a->positionnement} line(s) restored, {$a->positionnementlaissees} left as they were (a key that already holds a line here, a record or a rank this site does not hold, or a line already here). They are positionings of the structure, not validations.';
$string['importdossierselfpos'] = 'Self-positioning of the vaeiste: {$a->autopositionnement} line(s) restored, {$a->autopositionnementlaissees} left as they were (a line already here, a record or a node this site does not hold, or a node that already holds as many lines as it may). It is the vaeiste\'s own word, not a validation.';
$string['importdossiersituations'] = 'Work situations: {$a->situations} element(s) restored (whole situations, pieces, annotations, lines of consent), {$a->situationslaissees} left as they were (a situation: slot already taken, identifier already here, a record this site does not hold or too many versions; a tag or a link to a piece this site does not hold, the situation coming back without them; a piece, an annotation or a consent: identifier already here or a bound reached). The annotations and the consents restored name no account of this site and open no annotation; nothing is a validation.';
$string['importdossierwithdrawnotice'] = 'Attestations carried in from an archive are tied to no account of this site. Only the site administrator may withdraw them.';
$string['importencoding'] = 'File encoding';
$string['importencoding_help'] = 'The character encoding of the deposited file. UTF-8 is what most tools export today; a spreadsheet on Windows often writes Windows-1252 instead. Choosing the wrong one does not stop the import: it strips the accents from every label, silently. If the labels come out mangled, remove the framework of the record in Site administration, Competencies, Competency frameworks (possible as long as no candidate has declared against it), then import it again with the other encoding.';
$string['importfichecode'] = 'Record code';
$string['importfichecode_help'] = 'The code of the certification record, for example RNCP36832 or RS5678. It is what a re-import matches on, so it never changes for a given record.';
