$string['privacy:metadata:consent'] = 'The consent the vaeiste gives, by name, to a manager who follows them, to annotate their work situations and their self-positioning (lot 1b). Written by the vaeiste alone; added to and never changed: the latest line of a couple says whether it stands. A line restored from an archive names the manager by an opaque identifier and never opens the annotation. The line is deleted when the manager it names is erased: a consent given to nobody has no meaning.';
$string['privacy:metadata:consent:candidateid'] = 'The vaeiste, the only author of the line.';
$string['privacy:metadata:consent:importedat'] = 'When the line was restored from an archive; empty for a line written here.';
$string['privacy:metadata:consent:managerid'] = 'The manager the consent is given to. Empty for a line restored from an archive; the line is deleted when that person is erased.';
$string['privacy:metadata:consent:manageruuid'] = 'The opaque identifier of the manager of a line restored from an archive; empty for a line written here. The line is deleted when that person is erased.';
$string['privacy:metadata:consent:state'] = 'Whether the consent is given or withdrawn by this line.';
$string['privacy:metadata:consent:timecreated'] = 'When the line was written.';
$string['privacy:metadata:consent:uuid'] = 'The identifier of the line, as it is written in the archive.';
$string['privacy:metadata:core_ai'] = 'The text a candidate sends to the reformulation aid, and the answer, go to the AI provider the site chose and are kept by the core in its own tables, tied to the site\'s context in the candidate\'s name (not to their user context, which the core deletes after the account); the privacy provider of the core treats them. This plugin erases none of them itself, at the deletion of the account or at any other time: they are emptied, with the person\'s other text-generation actions in that context, when a person approves the data deletion request that Moodle files at each deletion of an account, on two conditions: that the site files these requests on its own, and that the purpose and the category of the site are not defined in its data registry (once they are, Moodle never empties these texts, even when the request is approved and declared done, and they have to be erased by hand). In every case the core keeps a line of its register after the erasure: the account number, the date, the provider, the model, the size of the exchange (in tokens), the success or the failure of the call and, after a failure, the error message of the provider.';
$string['privacy:metadata:corecompetency'] = 'This plugin causes the competency subsystem to record prior-learning evidence on the candidate\'s behalf. The evidence itself, and any files attached to it, are held by that subsystem. It also reads the learning plans and course competencies of the core to show them to the candidate, and the names and statuses of the learning plans to the manager who follows the candidate when the core lets that manager read them. For the direction it reads, per certification record, the number of learning plans of the accounts that left a trace in the plugin (a declaration, an "outside my activity" mark or a validation preparation) and that are not deleted; drafts are counted, and no name and no identifier is read. It also reads the activities that carry a competency, with their course, as it reads the courses: the offer of training, with no data about a person.';
$string['privacy:metadata:corefiles'] = 'The files attached as supporting pieces are stored by the file subsystem in the candidate\'s user context. Exported dossier archives are stored there too: the archive the candidate exports themself is kept as long as the account exists (a new export replaces it), and the one another person exports is deleted after 24 hours. Backups of a dossier are kept without a time limit in the private files of the administrator who took them, and the weekly copies in those of the candidate; they are deleted with the dossier, when the candidate\'s account is deleted or the candidate asks to be forgotten.';
$string['privacy:metadata:coremessage'] = 'Notifications are sent through the messaging subsystem when a declaration awaits an attestation, when an attestation is recorded or withdrawn, when a competency leaves its certification record, when a manager asks a candidate for a precision on a declaration, when declarations have waited for an attestation for the number of days the administrator chose, when a manager asks a signatory to withdraw an attestation or the signatory refuses, when a declaration a signatory had attested is destroyed with the evidence record that held it, when a manager the vaeiste allowed writes an annotation on one of their work situations or on their self-positioning (to the vaeiste, without the manager\'s name nor the text of the annotation), and when the vaeiste consents to a manager annotating (to that manager, with the vaeiste\'s name). They name the candidate and the reference of the competency, never the content of a declaration nor of an annotation. Two of them name a manager: the one who asks, to the signatory they ask, and the managers who take over after a withdrawal, to the candidate. All are sent by the site\'s no-reply user, never in a person\'s name. Notifications are kept and erased by the messaging subsystem on its own schedule.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit'] = 'A deposit of the dossier de faisabilité or of the preparation of the validation dossier (free text analysing the own practice of the person): a dated snapshot of the latest saved version of every section, never changed afterwards. It may hold a date of birth and a nationality, like the sections it copies.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:candidateid'] = 'The candidate who made the deposit.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:content'] = 'The snapshot: the code, place, version and text or values of every section saved at that time.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:contenthash'] = 'The SHA-256 digest of the snapshot.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:doctype'] = 'The document deposited.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:note'] = 'An optional sentence the candidate wrote with the deposit.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:number'] = 'The number of the deposit for this candidate.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:timecreated'] = 'When the deposit was made.';
$string['privacy:metadata:deposit:uuid'] = 'The identifier this plugin gives the deposit.';
$string['privacy:metadata:draft'] = 'A section of a document the vaeiste writes (the dossier of feasibility, or the preparation of the validation dossier), with the draft in progress. A narrative describes what the professional did, never who it was done for; the sections of separate fields hold the vaeiste\'s own identity (birth name, date of birth, nationality, levels and titles of certifications, status). The sections of the preparation of the validation dossier describe work situations and can, despite the reminder, hold elements about the people supported or about colleagues; drafts and every saved version are kept. The sections by bloc are carried by the vaeiste\'s export and by the Word/ODT and PDF copies made for the vaeiste (the one in their private files, the one they download), never by the export of a third party, the copies a third party opens nor the backups; the text of a work situation (draft in progress and versions) goes into the vaeiste\'s export, the export of a third party who may read the preparation and the backups (file situations.json), never into the Word/ODT copies nor the PDF.';
